  "rules": [
    "Scan every required station each reporting cycle, regardless of known advertiser activity.",
    "The automatic station pass occurs before advertiser-specific or discrepancy-driven searching.",
    "Search each station political-file index for the full reporting window plus an overlap for late uploads and revisions.",
    "Queue exact contracts/orders/invoices and material revisions; record NAB/traffic-only filings as presence signals when no priced document is available.",
    "A station with multiple major-network affiliations on subchannels is scanned once at the FCC facility level, but all political-file folders must be considered.",
    "Shared-newsroom or independent local-news stations remain mandatory because political inventory can be placed there even without a Big Four affiliation.",
    "Include Spanish-language local-news outlets where they are distinct FCC facilities.",
    "Do not declare a market inactive until every required station plus known cable/DBS distributors has been checked.",
    "If a station changes call sign, affiliation, ownership, or FCC entity ID, update this manifest and alias table rather than silently dropping it.",
    "After a station's FCC entity/facility ID is positively resolved, persist it as station metadata so subsequent cycles do not rediscover identity from scratch."
  ]
